	<span>
		A practical rule-of-thumb:
	</span>
</h3>
<p><strong>Use attributions when you need=E2=80=A6</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>fast, per-example debugging</li>
<li>token-level evidence (spurious words, shortcuts)</li>
<li>explanations you can show to non-technical stakeholders</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Use concept methods when you need=E2=80=A6</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>representation-level analysis (=E2=80=9Cwhat features exist inside the =
model?=E2=80=9D)</li>
<li>reusable semantic factors across many examples</li>
<li>deeper inspection of internal mechanisms</li>
</ul>
<p>Interpreto is explicitly designed to offer both families as complementar=
y tools.</p>
<p>In the following parts, we details what is Attribution et Concept Based =
methods.</p>
