	<span>
		1) The Interpreto attribution API
	</span>
</h2>
<p>In interpreto, as in other libraries for attribution methods, the attrib=
ution methods are called explainers. One need to first instantiate an expla=
iner with the model, tokenizer, and method parameters, then compute the att=
ribution on a batch of inputs.</p>
<p>The classic HuggingFace loading:</p>
<div class=3D"relative group repo-copy-code"><pre><code class=3D"language-p=
ython"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">from</span> transformers <span class=3D=
"hljs-keyword">import</span> AutoModelForSequenceClassification, AutoTokeni=
zer

<span class=3D"hljs-comment"># Load your Hugging Face model and tokenizer</=
span>
repo_id =3D <span class=3D"hljs-string">"textattack/bert-base-uncased-imdb"=
</span>
model =3D AutoModelForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained(repo_id)
