	</a>
	<span>
		2) Inference-based attribution methods
	</span>
</h2>
<p>These methods work by generating <strong>perturbed versions</strong> of =
the input and observing how the model output changes.</p>
<p>Interpreto currently provides the following inference-based attribution =
methods:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Occlusion</strong>: removes or masks tokens one at a time and m=
easures the impact on the output.</li>
<li><strong>LIME</strong>: fits a local linear surrogate model on randomly =
perturbed inputs.</li>
<li><strong>KernelSHAP</strong>: estimates Shapley-like token contributions=
 via weighted regression.</li>
<li><strong>Sobol</strong>: performs variance-based sensitivity analysis, c=
apturing main effects and interactions.</li>
</ul>
<p>All these methods rely on explicit perturbations and do not require grad=
ient access, making them compatible with a wide range of models.</p>
<hr>
