	</a>
	<span>
		Step 2: Learn a concept space (concept models)
	</span>
</h2>
<p>Interpreto supports many concept-based explainers by wrapping <a href=3D=
"https://github.com/KempnerInstitute/overcomplete" rel=3D"nofollow"><code>o=
vercomplete</code></a> library.</p>
<p>The concept explainer is basically the link between a <code>model_with_s=
plit_points</code> (I -&gt; A -&gt; O) and the <code>concept_model</code> (=
A -&gt; C) and (C -&gt; A*).</p>
<div class=3D"relative group repo-copy-code"><pre><code class=3D"language-p=
ython"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">from</span> interpreto.concepts <span c=
lass=3D"hljs-keyword">import</span> SemiNMFConcepts

<span class=3D"hljs-comment"># 2 Instantiate and train the concept model</s=
pan>
explainer =3D SemiNMFConcepts(model_with_split_points, nb_concepts=3D<span =
class=3D"hljs-number">20</span>)  <span class=3D"hljs-comment"># usually ge=
nerative models need much more concepts.</span>
explainer.fit(activations)
</code></pre><button class=3D"absolute top-3 right-3 transition opacity-0 g=
roup-hover:opacity-80"><svg class=3D"" xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"=
 aria-hidden=3D"true" fill=3D"currentColor" focusable=3D"false" role=3D"img=
" width=3D"0.9em" height=3D"0.9em" preserveAspectRatio=3D"xMidYMid meet" vi=
ewBox=3D"0 0 32 32"><path d=3D"M28,10V28H10V10H28m0-2H10a2,2,0,0,0-2,2V28a2=
,2,0,0,0,2,2H28a2,2,0,0,0,2-2V10a2,2,0,0,0-2-2Z" transform=3D"translate(0)"=
></path><path d=3D"M4,18H2V4A2,2,0,0,1,4,2H18V4H4Z" transform=3D"translate(=
0)"></path><rect fill=3D"none" width=3D"32" height=3D"32"></rect></svg></bu=
tton></div>
<p>The following concept decomposition methods are currently available in I=
nterpreto:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Vanilla SAE</strong>: learns sparse latent directions via recon=
struction with an L1 sparsity constraint.</li>
<li><strong>JumpReLU SAE</strong>: variant of SAE using JumpReLU activation=
s to enforce stronger sparsity and interpretability.</li>
<li><strong>TopK SAE</strong>: sparse autoencoder where only the top-K acti=
vations are kept per input.</li>
<li><strong>BatchTopK SAE</strong>: TopK sparse autoencoder where sparsity =
is enforced at the batch level rather than per sample.</li>
<li><strong>KMeans</strong>: clusters activations into discrete groups, eac=
h cluster center acting as a concept.</li>
<li><strong>SVD</strong>: singular value decomposition extracting orthogona=
l directions that capture maximal variance.</li>
<li><strong>PCA</strong>: linear dimensionality reduction used as a simple,=
 non-sparse baseline.</li>
<li><strong>ICA</strong>: independent component analysis to extract statist=
ically independent latent directions.</li>
<li><strong>NMF</strong>: non-negative matrix factorization enforcing addit=
ive, parts-based representations.</li>
<li><strong>Semi-NMF</strong>: NMF variant allowing mixed-sign activations =
while keeping non-negative concept bases.</li>
<li><strong>ConvexNMF</strong>: NMF variant where concepts are constrained =
to be convex combinations of input activations.</li>
<li><strong>Neurons as Concepts</strong>: directly treats individual neuron=
s or embedding dimensions as concepts.</li>
<li><strong>Optimization-based decompositions (<code>optim</code>)</strong>=
: generic optimization framework for learning concept directions under cust=
om objectives.</li>
</ul>
