	<span>
		Step 4: Estimate concept importance on the output
	</span>
</h2>
<p>With concepts and their interpretations, we still do not know:</p>
<ul>
<li>=E2=80=9CWhich concepts is the class A built on?=E2=80=9D</li>
<li>=E2=80=9CWhich concepts impacted this prediction?=E2=80=9D</li>
</ul>
<p>To do so, we compute the <strong>gradients between the concept space and=
 the model output</strong> (C -&gt; A -&gt; O). In particular, we compute t=
he gradients multiplied by the concepts activations.</p>
<p>This is the conceptual equivalent of token attributions, but in <strong>=
concept space</strong> rather than input space. We plan to add other attrib=
ution methods for this functionality later.</p>
